          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did tuṭaippam mean, and what did sīppu mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பசி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பசி (pasi) — \"hunger\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hunger as a thing that arrives, rather than something you are. Kannada makes it ಹಸಿವು (hasivu) — the p traded for h one more time, exactly as it was between பசு and ಹಸು. Telugu went elsewhere, to ఆకలి (ākali)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set பசி (pasi) beside பசு and only the last mark separates them: one ends on the ி, the other on the ு. They are not related, and the difference is worth practising until it stops needing thought."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five feelings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pasi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pasi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pasu, then pasi, and hold the two endings apart",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pasu*, then *pasi*, and hold the two endings apart]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does பசி (pasi) mean? (\"hunger\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
