          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தூக்கம் (tūkkam) — \"sleep\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sleep as a state — the sleep you get, lose, or need more of. Kannada ನಿದ್ದೆ (nidde) and Telugu నిద్ర (nidra) both took the Sanskrit word; Tamil kept its own and stayed out of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Open it on a long ஊ, the same long ஊ that opens ஊசி, and then hold the க்க twice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
