          "title": "You'll want to know: காய்ச்சல்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "காய்ச்சல் (kāyccal) — \"a fever\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The body running hot. Tamil built the word on its own idea of heating rather than importing one, which is why it looks nothing like Kannada's ಜ್ವರ (jvara), taken straight from the Sanskrit."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the first thing anybody tells a மருத்துவர், and it is said flatly, the way you would report weather."
            }
          ]
        },
